  "answer": "The evidence does not describe an `ERR-ACL-MISMATCH` error code. In the documented incident, the subsystem that failed was the **document ingestion and indexing pipeline**: the document ingestion microservice and its Celery/Redis-backed import workers became unresponsive because a schema migration acquired an `AccessExclusiveLock` on `document_metadata`, triggering an uncapped retry storm that exhausted the PostgreSQL connection pool [NL-013#NL-013-S01] [NL-013#NL-013-S03] [NL-013#NL-013-S04].\n\nImmediate engineering corrective actions were: rollback of the configuration deploy, throttling database traffic, flushing the retry queue, restarting import workers, and temporarily raising the connection limit from 150 to 200 [NL-013#NL-013-S03] [NL-013#NL-013-S07]. Immediate customer-support actions were: status-page updates, a Zendesk auto-responder message, and follow-up notifications to all 17 affected customer accounts, including direct calls to BrightPath Healthcare and Northstar Financial [NL-013#NL-013-S06] [NL-013#NL-013-S02].\n\nBecause `ERR-ACL-MISMATCH` is not referenced in the evidence, no specific ACL-mismatch remediation can be cited.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
